# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The problem this solves: Astro fingerprints CSS and JS filenames on every
# build. If a browser caches the HTML, that stale HTML keeps asking for asset
# filenames that no longer exist, and the page renders with no styling or
# inert widgets. That is why a hard refresh has been needed after every deploy.
#
# The fix is the standard pairing for fingerprinted assets:
#   HTML   — never cached, so a visitor always gets markup pointing at files
#            that actually exist.
#   Assets — cached forever, safe precisely because the filename changes
#            whenever the contents do.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# Fingerprinted build output — the filename changes when the content does,
# so this can be cached indefinitely.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Word-game dictionaries. Large, and regenerated only when the source list
# changes, so a day of caching is a reasonable compromise.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Everything else is HTML. Revalidate every time.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
